To resolve the "blank PDF" and broken print functionality, I need to restructure how the print view is rendered.

**The Problem:**
1.  **PDF:** `html2pdf.js` takes a "screenshot" of the DOM element. Because the element was positioned off-screen (`left: -10000px`) or hidden, the screenshot engine (`html2canvas`) captured an empty or clipped image.
2.  **Print:** The CSS `visibility: hidden` approach can be flaky with deep React component nesting, sometimes creating blank pages because the parent containers still take up layout space even if invisible.

**The Solution:**
1.  **For PDF:** When you click "Download PDF", I will temporarily force the print view to be **visible and overlaid** on top of the app (fullscreen white background). This ensures the PDF generator sees exactly what it needs to see. Once the download starts, it reverts to hidden.
2.  **For Print:** I will refine the `@media print` CSS to ensure the print container is positioned absolutely at the top-left of the document, bypassing any layout constraints of the app.

# Updated files:

## index.html

Updated CSS to handle printing more robustly.

```html
<style>
    /* ... existing styles ... */

    @media print {
      @page { margin: 0.5in; }

      /* Robust Print Reset */
      body {
        visibility: hidden;
        background: white;
      }

      /* Only show the print root and its children */
      #print-root, #print-root * {
        visibility: visible;
      }

      #print-root {
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        top: 0;
        width: 100%;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: block !important;
      }

      /* Hide everything else specifically to collapse layout space */
      body > *:not(#root) {
        display: none;
      }
      #root {
        display: contents; /* Allows children to break out of root flow */
      }

      /* Hide non-print UI inside the app */
      .no-print {
        display: none !important;
      }
    }
</style>
```

## components/BookReader.tsx

Updated the logic to "Mount" the print view visibly during PDF generation to guarantee `html2pdf` can capture it.

```tsx

To implement the Series functionality, persistent Context (Bible), and the ability to edit/regenerate content more flexibly, I will update the application structure.

Here is the plan:
1.  **`types.ts`**: Add `BookSeries`, `SeriesContext` (Characters, Settings), and update `BookProject`.
2.  **`services/gemini.ts`**: Update generation functions to accept and utilize the `SeriesContext` so characters remain consistent.
3.  **`components/SeriesBible.tsx`**: A new component to manage Characters and Settings.
4.  **`components/SeriesView.tsx`**: A new view to manage a specific series, its books, and its bible.
5.  **`components/Dashboard.tsx`**: Add tabs to switch between Projects and Series, and logic to create Series.
6.  **`components/BookReader.tsx`**: Add "Edit Mode" to allow manual rewriting of AI output, and "Regenerate" functionality.
7.  **`components/ProjectEditor.tsx`**: Integrate Series Context injection and allow jumping back to the Outline step to edit and re-run generation.
8.  **`App.tsx`**: Manage the new Series state and navigation hierarchy.

